#N canvas 20 20 7000 11860 12;
#X text 20 20 midi-bench -- the MIDI acceptance run: the mode-dependent map \, both output devices and the SP-404 in both directions. MOST OF THIS IS PROVEN HEADLESSLY -- test/gate/sp404-assert.sh asserts all sixteen pads \, the rate limiter and the allowlist guard in about eight seconds \, and test/gate/map-assert.sh asserts the lookup. What is left here is only what HARDWARE can show: a real pad under a real finger \, and a Volca you can hear. STEPPED BY HAND: press GO to run the step that has just been described \, press GO again to describe the next one. Nothing moves until you ask it to \, so the PASS IF is on screen and STILL while you read it. The prompt line always says what the next press will do., f 120;
#X text 20 150 GO ON THE MAC: the bng below \, or the dev panel's ENCODER CLICK -- u_mother-stub sends encbut unconditionally and nothing in Cut It consumes it. TURNING the encoder repeats the current step without advancing \, which is what to do when you looked away., f 120;
#X text 2400 200 ⚠️ GO ON THE DEVICE IS NOT THE ENCODER -- IT IS netcat \, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT OPTIONAL. mother only forwards encbut once a patch has asked with /enableEncoder \, and NOTHING IN Cut It EVER ASKS -- m_organelle leaves the encoder out on purpose. So the click that drives this bench on the Mac is silently dead on the Organelle. Send instead with ./test/run.sh --bench <name> from the Mac. ⚠️ NOT netcat: the line this file used to print does nothing on macOS -- BSD nc exits before the datagram is flushed at -w0 \, and -w1 was measured to fail too \, while the port IS bound and the bench is fine. It looks exactly like a dead bench. The device cannot send to itself either: busybox here has no nc at all. Asking mother to enable the encoder is NOT the fix either: that means writing to oscOut \, and g_oled is its sole owner., f 120;
#X text 20 280 Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch -- it only pushes onto the same buses a controller would. A PASS IF is printed for EVERY step including the ones whose correct result is that nothing happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark off., f 120;
#X text 2400 20 ON THE MAC EVERY ERROR STEP ALSO PRINTS /sdcard/cut-it-err.cur: write failed \, AND THAT IS NOT A FAILED STEP. u_err keeps its durable log on the Organelle's SD card \, which no Mac has -- so the write is attempted and refused every time. It is in fact the only proof off-device that the logging path ran at all. On the device that line must NOT appear \, and if it does the card is unwritable and the log is being lost silently., f 120;
#X obj 6000 40 r \$0-say;
#X obj 6000 100 print;
#X text 20 360 GO -- click here \, or the dev panel's encoder button. MAC ONLY -- on the device use netcat \, top right., f 60;
#X obj 20 420 bng 40 250 50 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 20 500 s \$0-go;
#X obj 300 420 r encbut;
#X obj 300 480 select 1;
#X obj 300 540 t b;
#X obj 300 600 s \$0-go;
#X text 560 480 encbut sends 1 THEN 0 \, so select 1 is what stops one press counting twice., f 46;
#X obj 300 680 netreceive 9998 1;
#X obj 300 740 route go rerun where show;
#X obj 300 800 t b;
#X obj 300 860 s \$0-go;
#X obj 620 800 t b;
#X obj 620 860 s \$0-rerun;
#X text 860 800 rerun fires the CURRENT step again without advancing \, so a visual step can be looked at more than once. [r]epeat in test/run.sh sends it., f 46;
#X obj 1500 800 t b b;
#X obj 1680 860 f;
#X obj 1500 860 f;
#X obj 1500 920 pack f f;
#X obj 1500 980 print bench-at;
#X obj 1500 740 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1680 740 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 2000 800 t b;
#X obj 2000 860 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 2200 800 show goes through $0-repeat \, which is the encoder's path too -- one way to re-describe a step \, not two., f 46;
#X obj 1400 420 r enc;
#X obj 1400 480 t b;
#X obj 1400 540 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 1660 480 enc is 1 for up and 0 for down -- not plus or minus one -- so either direction repeats., f 46;
#X text 20 920 THE STATE MACHINE. phase 0 means the step has been described and not yet run \; phase 1 means it has run. SETTING THE STEP NUMBER IS WHAT DESCRIBES IT \, so advancing is just an increment -- there is no second path to keep in step., f 120;
#X obj 20 980 r \$0-go;
#X obj 20 1040 f;
#X obj 20 1100 select 0 1;
#X obj 300 1040 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1170 t b b;
#X msg 300 1230 1;
#X obj 300 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1290 f;
#X obj 20 1350 s \$0-do-run;
#X obj 20 1230 r \$0-rerun;
#X obj 900 1170 t b b;
#X msg 1180 1230 0;
#X obj 1180 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 900 1350 f;
#X obj 900 1410 + 1;
#X obj 900 1470 s \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 980 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 1040 t f f f;
#X obj 1700 1110 s \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 1980 1110 s \$0-set-run;
#X obj 1180 1350 r \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 300 1410 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2260 1110 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2600 980 r \$0-repeat;
#X obj 2600 1040 f;
#X obj 2780 980 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2600 1100 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 3100 980 loadbang;
#X obj 3100 1040 del 500;
#X msg 3100 1100 1;
#X obj 3100 1160 s \$0-set-step;
#X text 20 1920 DESCRIBING A STEP. One select per step rather than one wide fan \, so every cord stays short and local -- the same reason u_map chains its routes., f 120;
#X obj 20 2020 r \$0-do-show;
#X obj 20 2080 select 1;
#X obj 240 2080 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2080 === STEP-01-of-18 === Restored tempo at boot;
#X msg 700 2130 PASS IF: The footer reads 57 BPM and not 120 BPM. The lit mode lamp is wherever you left it -- note which one it is.;
#X msg 700 2180 >>> press GO to run step 1 of 18;
#X obj 240 2250 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2340 select 2;
#X obj 240 2340 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2340 === STEP-02-of-18 === Get to mode 1;
#X msg 700 2390 PASS IF: The lit lamp moves to the first position. Nothing below works until it does.;
#X msg 700 2440 >>> press GO to run step 2 of 18;
#X obj 240 2510 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2600 select 3;
#X obj 240 2600 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2600 === STEP-03-of-18 === SP-404 pad 1;
#X msg 700 2650 PASS IF: The OLED shows sp-bank 1 and sp-pad 1 together.;
#X msg 700 2700 >>> press GO to run step 3 of 18;
#X obj 240 2770 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2860 select 4;
#X obj 240 2860 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2860 === STEP-04-of-18 === SP-404 pad 5;
#X msg 700 2910 PASS IF: sp-pad reads 5 on the OLED. Anything else is the failure.;
#X msg 700 2960 >>> press GO to run step 4 of 18;
#X obj 240 3030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3120 select 5;
#X obj 240 3120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3120 === STEP-05-of-18 === All sixteen pads;
#X msg 700 3170 PASS IF: sp-pad counts 1 2 3 up to 16 in step with your finger while sp-bank stays at 1 throughout. A run that counts 1 2 3 4 and then jumps is the failure.;
#X msg 700 3220 >>> press GO to run step 5 of 18;
#X obj 240 3290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3380 select 6;
#X obj 240 3380 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3380 === STEP-06-of-18 === Bank B;
#X msg 700 3430 PASS IF: sp-pad still reads 1 but sp-bank changes from 1 to 2 as you switch banks.;
#X msg 700 3480 >>> press GO to run step 6 of 18;
#X obj 240 3550 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3640 select 7;
#X obj 240 3640 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3640 === STEP-07-of-18 === A release is not a press;
#X msg 700 3690 PASS IF: The sp-pad and sp-bank rows update on the press and neither updates again on the release. Exactly one sp-pad row per hit -- two is the failure.;
#X msg 700 3740 >>> press GO to run step 7 of 18;
#X obj 240 3810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3900 select 8;
#X obj 240 3900 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3900 === STEP-08-of-18 === Fader 1 in mode 1;
#X msg 700 3950 PASS IF: The Volca tone changes as you move it.;
#X msg 700 4000 >>> press GO to run step 8 of 18;
#X obj 240 4070 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4160 select 9;
#X obj 240 4160 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4160 === STEP-09-of-18 === Fader 1 in mode 4;
#X msg 700 4210 PASS IF: The Volca does not change -- no change is the pass. The OLED still shows the fader moving and that is correct.;
#X msg 700 4260 >>> press GO to run step 9 of 18;
#X obj 240 4330 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4420 select 10;
#X obj 240 4420 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4420 === STEP-10-of-18 === Fader 1 back in mode 1;
#X msg 700 4470 PASS IF: The Volca responds again. Still silent means the mode did not change back -- check the lit lamp.;
#X msg 700 4520 >>> press GO to run step 10 of 18;
#X obj 240 4590 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4680 select 11;
#X obj 240 4680 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4680 === STEP-11-of-18 === Tempo from knob 1;
#X msg 700 4730 PASS IF: The footer BPM follows the knob over roughly 10 to 500 BPM once the knob has crossed the restored value. Nothing at all happens before it crosses.;
#X msg 700 4780 >>> press GO to run step 11 of 18;
#X obj 240 4850 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4940 select 12;
#X obj 240 4940 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4940 === STEP-12-of-18 === Transport from the aux button;
#X msg 700 4990 PASS IF: The aux LED changes state on each press and the footer agrees.;
#X msg 700 5040 >>> press GO to run step 12 of 18;
#X obj 240 5110 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5200 select 13;
#X obj 240 5200 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5200 === STEP-13-of-18 === Panic is unbound;
#X msg 700 5250 PASS IF: Nothing on the rig can raise panic and nothing is meant to.;
#X msg 700 5300 >>> press GO to run step 13 of 18;
#X obj 240 5370 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5460 select 14;
#X obj 240 5460 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5460 === STEP-14-of-18 === Hot-swap -- SP-404 unplugged;
#X msg 700 5510 PASS IF: A bordered alert on the OLED reads warn and then m_404.;
#X msg 700 5560 >>> press GO to run step 14 of 18;
#X obj 240 5630 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5720 select 15;
#X obj 240 5720 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5720 === STEP-15-of-18 === Hot-swap -- SP-404 absent at load;
#X msg 700 5770 PASS IF: The OLED shows an sp-pad row.;
#X msg 700 5820 >>> press GO to run step 15 of 18;
#X obj 240 5890 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5980 select 16;
#X obj 240 5980 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5980 === STEP-16-of-18 === Hot-swap -- SP-404 unplugged and plugged back in;
#X msg 700 6030 PASS IF: The OLED shows an sp-pad row again.;
#X msg 700 6080 >>> press GO to run step 16 of 18;
#X obj 240 6150 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6240 select 17;
#X obj 240 6240 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6240 === STEP-17-of-18 === Hot-swap -- Volca unplugged and plugged back in;
#X msg 700 6290 PASS IF: Holding a Volca key and sweeping slider 1 changes the sound -- by ear.;
#X msg 700 6340 >>> press GO to run step 17 of 18;
#X obj 240 6410 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6500 select 18;
#X obj 240 6500 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6500 === STEP-18-of-18 === Hot-swap -- Volca absent at load;
#X msg 700 6550 PASS IF: Holding a Volca key and sweeping slider 1 changes the sound -- by ear. Sweep it up -- slider 1 is velocity.;
#X msg 700 6600 >>> press GO to run step 18 of 18;
#X obj 240 6670 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6760 t b;
#X msg 240 6760 === BENCH COMPLETE === every step has been run -- reload the patch to go round again;
#X obj 240 6820 s \$0-say;
